speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I rise to ask the unanimous consent of the House under Standing Order 43, to move a motion of urgent and pressing necessity arising from the failure as yet of the Minister of Transport (Mr. Marchand) to fulfil the commitment made to the House on January 16, 1973, through his parliamentary secretary, to give answers to questions raised concerning the environmental impact of the proposed new runway at Vancouver airport. I move, seconded by the hon. member for Burnaby-Richmond-Delta (Mr. Reynolds):
That in view of the commitment given this House on January 16, 1973, by the hon. the Parliamentary Secretary to the Minister of Transport, that if questions are raised regarding the environmental impact of the proposed new runway at Vancouver International Airport answers will be given;
And because this exact question was raised yesterday at the expropriation hearings presently being conducted at Vancouver;
That this House direct the Minister of Transport to immediately answer the question raised yesterday asking what the environmental impact of the proposed new runway will be, and to make such answer or answers available to the objectors and the public at the present hearings.

Mr. Speaker, in view of inadequacy of passenger service in southwestern Ontario and the delay of the government in moving to remedy this situation, I ask leave of the House to propose a motion

under Standing Order 43. I therefore move, seconded by the hon. member for Perth-Wilmot (Mr. Jarvis);
That this House urge the government to take immediate action to implement the recommendations contained in the report of the transport committee of the 28th parliament concerning passenger service in southwestern Ontario.
